From d778b0dc2ec3201bf4eb55cdcac942dd64baaa2d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: qwert-Xx <128706845+qwert-Xx@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 10:19:30 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fbdev: imx50-epdc: expose owned WB direct-drive sessions

Reserve a private synthetic waveform DMA table, derive A2 electrode actions at session startup, and drive fixed-color FULL updates on LUT0. Count EOF boundaries in IRQ context and restart completed LUTs in the owner worker. Exclude normal updates while the session owns the panel.

Separate mmap inode references from device fd ownership and revoke mappings before draining STOP. Restore full canvas history, including SNAPSHOT capture, after STOP; stop on last fd close, suspend and removal. Keep stopped core objects alive for outstanding device files.

Host ASan/UBSan image, pipeline (49/50 DMA debug scenarios), framebuffer, waveform, PxP and Papyrus power tests pass. ARM EPDC objects compile. Physical EOF timing and panel behavior require device validation.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
